{
  "$comment": [
    "THE RULE FOR A PER-CONVERSATION NICKNAME, written once and asserted by both implementations:",
    "the frontend's `normalizeNickname` (frontend/src/lib/utils/users/nicknameRules.ts), which every",
    "MLS group frame goes through on the way out and on the way in, and social-service's",
    "(apps/social-service/src/channels/community-nicknames.ts), which a community's column goes",
    "through. Each side's spec walks these cases, so the two cannot drift apart.",
    "",
    "Mirrors the profile's name fields (owner, 2026-10-14: the limits of a nickname are the profile's):",
    "NFKC, every control and format character dropped (zero-width, bidi overrides), trimmed, and at",
    "most `maxLength` CODE POINTS - the unit PostgreSQL's varchar counts, and the profile form's",
    "`maxlength` of 100. A value that is empty once normalized means NO nickname (a reset), never an",
    "empty one. `expected` null is that reset; `error` names the typed refusal."
  ],
  "maxLength": 100,
